WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The Oscars
are coming up this Sunday,

00:00:01.701 --> 00:00:03.103 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it has been a great year
for diversity in film,

00:00:03.103 --> 00:00:05.739
and with that in mind,
we have two very special guests

00:00:05.739 --> 00:00:06.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
from the American
Diversity Council,

00:00:06.940 --> 00:00:10.310 align:start size:94% position:6%
who are here today to honor
the most diverse film of 2018.

00:00:10.310 --> 00:00:13.847 align:start size:94% position:6%
Please welcome Linda Porter
and Peter Ralph.

00:00:13.847 --> 00:00:16.249 size:84% position:42% line:92%
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.249 --> 00:00:18.351 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you both so much
for being here.

00:00:18.351 --> 00:00:21.154 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It's good to be here, Seth.
-This is very exciting.

00:00:21.154 --> 00:00:24.057 align:start size:94% position:6%
Your organization's analysts
have crunched the numbers

00:00:24.057 --> 00:00:26.926
and determined the most diverse
movie of last year,

00:00:26.926 --> 00:00:29.095
and you're going to announce it
on the show tonight.

00:00:29.095 --> 00:00:33.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah. Uh, that's
what we're gonna do.

00:00:33.400 --> 00:00:34.334 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-So, what is it?

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:37.404 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Crazy Rich Asians"?
"Roma"? "Black Panther"?

00:00:37.404 --> 00:00:38.805 line:92%
-Look, Seth, I don't think

00:00:38.805 --> 00:00:40.407 align:start size:94% position:6%
you're gonna like
what we have to say.

00:00:40.407 --> 00:00:41.474 line:92%
-Yeah, I think it might be best

00:00:41.474 --> 00:00:43.443 size:78% position:39%
to just pull the plug
on this right now.

00:00:43.443 --> 00:00:45.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Are you kidding me?
No, this is really exciting.

00:00:45.612 --> 00:00:48.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
Diversity is very important.
Let's do it.

00:00:48.848 --> 00:00:50.683 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Fine. Okay.

00:00:50.683 --> 00:00:53.119 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Breathes deeply ]

00:00:53.119 --> 00:00:56.456 align:start size:94% position:6%
Seth, it is with some regret
that we have to announce

00:00:56.456 --> 00:00:59.392 align:start size:94% position:6%
that the most diverse movie
of 2018 is

00:00:59.392 --> 00:01:01.594 line:92%
"Backyard Bus Bangers 6."

00:01:01.594 --> 00:01:05.565 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.734 line:92%
-I'm sorry. What did you say?

00:01:07.734 --> 00:01:08.535 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:01:08.535 --> 00:01:10.503 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We at the American
Diversity Council

00:01:10.503 --> 00:01:14.641
used a highly scientific rubric
to determine which film released

00:01:14.641 --> 00:01:17.844
in the last year was
the most diverse and inclusive.

00:01:17.844 --> 00:01:21.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
Unfortunately,
that film turned out to be

00:01:21.514 --> 00:01:23.650 line:92%
"Backyard Bus Bangers 6."

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:28.621 align:start size:94% position:6%
The sixth movie in the
"Backyard Bus Bangers" series.

00:01:28.621 --> 00:01:31.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I gotta say,
that sounds like a --

00:01:31.224 --> 00:01:33.660 line:92%
-It is pornography, Seth.

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:37.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
But "Backyard Bus Bangers 6,"
I'm sorry to say,

00:01:37.097 --> 00:01:41.201
has a more diverse cast than
any other movie made in 2018.

00:01:41.201 --> 00:01:43.870 align:start size:94% position:6%
-The movie features
African-American actors,

00:01:43.870 --> 00:01:47.941
Hispanic actors, Indian actors,
Chinese actors.

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:50.176
-And there's really no easy way
to put this,

00:01:50.176 --> 00:01:53.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
but our study found
that "Backyard Bus Bangers 6"

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:56.649 align:start size:94% position:6%
features roughly nine times
more interracial relationships

00:01:56.649 --> 00:01:59.152 size:81% position:41%
than any other movie
made in the last year.

00:01:59.152 --> 00:02:04.324
-And when you include Jewish
director Hershel Thrust...

00:02:04.324 --> 00:02:07.560 align:start size:94% position:6%
the production
clearly embraced diversity

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:11.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
both in front of
and behind the camera.

00:02:11.564 --> 00:02:13.933 line:92%
-Does certainly sound diverse.

00:02:13.933 --> 00:02:15.468 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Also, it's worth noting
that while

00:02:15.468 --> 00:02:18.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nick Jonas and Priyanka Chopra
are not in this movie,

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:21.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
there is a couple that looks
almost exactly like them.

00:02:21.941 --> 00:02:28.148 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Their names are Prick Bonas
and Peeonya Chokeya.

00:02:28.148 --> 00:02:30.617 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:02:33.486 --> 00:02:35.188 line:92%
-Maybe you should move on.

00:02:35.188 --> 00:02:36.756 line:92%
How about a film that was good

00:02:36.756 --> 00:02:39.492 align:start size:94% position:6%
for LGBTQ representation
in 2018?

00:02:39.492 --> 00:02:42.662
-Well, I'm sure no one is
going to be happy to hear this,

00:02:42.662 --> 00:02:45.532 align:start size:94% position:6%
but we at the American
Diversity Council

00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:49.402
also found that there is no film
that more represents

00:02:49.402 --> 00:02:52.105 line:92%
the LGBTQ community than...

00:02:52.105 --> 00:02:54.507 line:92%
"Backyard Bus Bangers 6."

00:02:54.507 --> 00:02:56.342 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-God.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:59.512
-"Backyard Bus Bangers 6"
shows us that Hollywood romances

00:02:59.512 --> 00:03:02.115 align:start size:94% position:6%
doesn't have to be
the traditional male/female

00:03:02.115 --> 00:03:03.616 align:start size:94% position:6%
relationships we see
in most movies.

00:03:03.616 --> 00:03:08.254
-They can also be female/female
or female/female/male.

00:03:08.254 --> 00:03:09.756 size:88% position:44% line:92%
Or female/female/female.

00:03:09.756 --> 00:03:12.091 line:92%
Or female/female/female/female.

00:03:12.091 --> 00:03:15.328 align:start size:94% position:6%
-What about male/male
relationships?

00:03:15.328 --> 00:03:16.462 line:92%
-While there's technically

00:03:16.462 --> 00:03:18.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
no male/male relationship
in the movie,

00:03:18.464 --> 00:03:24.604
there is a scene -- and, uh,
I think it was an accident --

00:03:24.604 --> 00:03:27.941 line:92%
where two guys, um, touched.

00:03:27.941 --> 00:03:30.476 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:03:33.479 --> 00:03:37.584
-Where can people watch
"Backyard Bus Bangers 6?"

00:03:37.584 --> 00:03:40.153 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, it's currently
in wide release

00:03:40.153 --> 00:03:43.156
to all Starwood Hotel and Resort
properties.

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:48.294
And I believe it premieres
on Showtime Extreme in June.

00:03:48.294 --> 00:03:49.562 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-That's great.

00:03:49.562 --> 00:03:50.496 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah.
-Uh-huh.

00:03:50.496 --> 00:03:54.067 align:start size:94% position:6%
So congratulations
to the cast and crew

00:03:54.067 --> 00:03:56.636 line:92%
of "Backyard Bus Bangers 6."

00:03:56.636 --> 00:03:57.770 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I shudder to say

00:03:57.770 --> 00:04:01.474 align:start size:94% position:6%
that more Hollywood films
should aspire to your example.

00:04:01.474 --> 00:04:02.308 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.308 --> 00:04:08.781
-This is a, you know,
a great day for representation.

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.751 line:92%
-Huge win for inclusivity.

00:04:11.751 --> 00:04:14.287 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
[ Laughter ]

00:04:15.855 --> 00:04:20.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Out of curiosity, what was
the second-most diverse movie?

00:04:20.727 --> 00:04:25.331
-Unfortunately, it was
"Backyard Bus Bangers 7."

00:04:25.331 --> 00:04:27.734 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And that came out
in the same year?

00:04:27.734 --> 00:04:29.502
-I think they were actually
filmed on the same weekend.

00:04:29.502 --> 00:04:33.506
-Okay. Gotcha. Give it up for
the American Diversity Council!

